&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great AI doesn’t start with a great model. It starts with a great platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The success of an AI initiative is rarely determined by the model alone. More often, it depends on the quality of the platform underneath it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Platform Engineer in our central Data &amp;amp; AI team, you’ll build the foundations that let engineers develop, deploy and operate AI workloads safely and efficiently. You’ll work on the infrastructure, automation and platform capabilities that allow teams to innovate without compromising reliability, and you’ll bridge the gap between promising technology and production reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think Kubernetes platforms, deployment automation, observability, security and developer experience. Think AI workloads built around Large Language Models, retrieval systems, graph technologies and modern data platforms. Think creating an environment where engineers focus on solving problems rather than fighting infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing self-service platform capabilities using Kubernetes, Terraform and GitOps principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalizing graph and vector databases, and enabling model serving workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the observability of AI systems running in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating OpenAI or Anthropic-based services into our platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalizing LangGraph workloads on Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling GraphRAG architectures powered by Neo4j&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing deployment patterns so AI services meet the same standards as any other production workload&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll spend less time tuning models and more time making sure AI capabilities can be trusted, operated and continuously improved. This role sits at the intersection of platform engineering, software engineering and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis we don’t believe in throwing solutions over the fence. The engineers building systems are responsible for running them too, and that ownership extends to AI just as much as every other technology we work with. Your impact won’t be measured by the number of clusters you manage, but by how much autonomy and confidence other engineers gain from the platform you’ve built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to meet you if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care deeply about building platforms that other engineers love to use, and you’re happiest when automation replaces repetitive work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong background in Platform Engineering, SRE, infrastructure or distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have extensive experience building and operating Kubernetes-based and cloud-native environments, with infrastructure automation at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built and operated production environments using tools such as Terraform, ArgoCD, GitHub Actions or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand what it takes to operationalize AI workloads in production, and technologies such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Neo4j, GraphRAG, vector databases or LangGraph are familiar territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You believe observability, reliability and security belong in every design conversation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy improving developer experience through automation and self-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see the gap between a successful proof of concept and a production-ready system and immediately start figuring out how to close it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership of the result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You get satisfaction from enabling other engineers to move faster and safer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently based in the Netherlands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions? Please do not hesitate to contact Maggie: 0623757086&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Only applications submitted through the website will be considered.&amp;nbsp;Please note that we do not work with external recruitment agencies and we will not pay any fees for unrequested CV introductions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Description:&lt;/strong&gt; Systemiq is a system-change company committed to achieving the Sustainable Development Goals and the Paris Agreement by transforming markets and business models across five key systems: nature and food, materials and circularity, energy, urban areas, and sustainable finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a certified B Corp, we combine strategic advisory with high-impact, on-the-ground work, partnering with business, finance, policymakers and civil society to deliver system change. With offices across Africa, Asia, Europe and the Americas, we are dedicated exclusively to sustainability-focused work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strategy Associate, Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: London preferred. Amsterdam also possible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Systemiq is looking for a Strategy Associate to join our Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy team. This role is suited to someone who combines strong strategic thinking with the intellectual curiosity to tackle complex sustainability challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on some of the most important questions facing companies, governments and wider society as they shift towards more circular and sustainable models. Projects can range from shaping corporate strategy and identifying new business opportunities to assessing value chains, developing policy recommendations and designing system-level interventions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can bring the core toolkit and pace of a strong strategy consultant: structured problem-solving, analytical rigour, clear communication and sound judgement. Strategy consulting experience is one route to demonstrating this. We are equally interested in candidates from other demanding analytical environments who can show the same quality of thinking and ability to turn complexity into clear recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join small, senior-led project teams and take meaningful responsibility from the outset. You will structure problems, conduct analysis, develop insights and work directly with clients to translate those insights into practical strategic choices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structure complex problems:&lt;/strong&gt; break ambiguous questions into clear workstreams, hypotheses and analytical priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate insights:&lt;/strong&gt; conduct rigorous qualitative and quantitative analysis, drawing conclusions from incomplete or complex information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape recommendations:&lt;/strong&gt; translate analysis into clear, concise and practical strategic recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop client materials:&lt;/strong&gt; produce high-quality presentations, briefings and other client-ready outputs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with clients:&lt;/strong&gt; work directly with senior stakeholders across businesses, governments, foundations and non-governmental organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to project direction:&lt;/strong&gt; help shape project approaches, hypotheses and emerging strategic conclusions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build trusted relationships:&lt;/strong&gt; work effectively with clients, partners and stakeholders across multi-organisation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be part of Systemiq&#39;s Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy platform, led by Partner Ben Dixon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ben works across circular economy and energy topics and has advised organisations including the Ellen MacArthur Foundation, the United Nations International Resource Panel and multinational companies across packaging, chemicals and related sectors. He also leads Systemiq&#39;s work on plastics, focused on accelerating the transition towards a more circular and resource-efficient plastics system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Strategy and analytical capability&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for candidates who already demonstrate, or can quickly operate with, the core toolkit expected in strategy consulting. You should be able to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Structure complex and ambiguous problems into clear components, hypotheses and analytical questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply strong analytical judgement to qualitative and quantitative information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Synthesize complex material into concise insights and decision-relevant recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicate clearly in writing and verbally, including through high-quality presentation materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work effectively at pace, managing changing priorities and imperfect information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Move comfortably between detailed analysis and the broader strategic question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience and background&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will typically bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least two years of experience in strategy consulting, advisory or another analytically demanding environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evidence of strong performance and increasing responsibility in your previous roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience contributing to strategy, investment, commercial or other decision-focused work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong academic achievement, typically including a Master&#39;s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We particularly welcome candidates from strategy consulting, but relevant experience could also come from corporate strategy, investing, high-growth businesses, specialist advisory firms or other project-based environments where structured thinking and analytical rigour are central to the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Sector interest and understanding&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be a specialist across every part of the Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy agenda. You should, however, bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An understanding of, or demonstrated ability to learn, complex industrial and consumer value chains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exposure to sectors such as plastics, petrochemicals, chemicals, consumer goods, manufacturing, mobility, energy or waste management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong interest in sustainability, circular economy and the economic and strategic questions involved in system change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Location&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London is the preferred location for this role. We would also consider Amsterdam for candidates whose experience and capabilities are an especially strong match for the position.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;description__body&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;578&quot; data-end=&quot;603&quot;&gt;Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br data-start=&quot;603&quot; data-end=&quot;606&quot;&gt;At Systemiq, we absolutely believe diverse perspectives are essential to driving system change. We are committed to creating an inclusive workplace where people feel respected, supported and able to do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.systemiq.earth/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to view our Data Policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;At IMC, technology is not a department; it’s at the heart of everything we do. Developed in house, our innovative software makes millions of trading decisions daily, and we win by making better and faster decisions than our competition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IMC’s Amsterdam-based Global VMM Data team works on a centralised global data platform to serve high-quality curated data for Valuation Market Making (VMM) research and strategies all throughout IMC. We address the ever changing data requirements and our team tries to solve this in a young project building a central system to ingest, curate and expose data to our research tooling within IMC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Core Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Trading Data Software Engineer, you&#39;ll work on enabling high-quality research using fundamental option pricing data. Next to that you will increase researchers&#39; focus by centralising the curation of the data and enable quick onboarding of new data sets, to allow for researching new types of strategies that are going to play a vital role in the strategies of IMC now and in the future. We build the tooling that allows a team of data curators to perform their magic and on top of that we expose our data to research tooling to provide a global access.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll write reliable, high-performance software while balancing time to production with quality and testability. Advanced automated testing and daily deployments will allow you to achieve agile and incremental benefits. Within the complex landscape of IMC and its systems and technologies, you’ll be constantly challenged to consider trade-offs between latency, throughput, simplicity, scalability and maintainability. Your core tasks will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coding, developing, testing, deploying and maintaining applications and automations for data curators, other VMM developers and Traders/researchers to support them and understand their actual needs and the data we serve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on a young project and being involved of the architectural design of our system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building a system that is highly-performant at serving petabytes of data globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least &amp;gt; 4 years of experience as a Software Engineer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Java (11+), but experience in the latest versions of Java is highly desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Docker, Kubernetes and&amp;nbsp;Linux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills with Python, especially around data - highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in data analysis and building out data platforms and data - highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability able to work under minimal supervision and to take full ownership of the applications you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting and diagnostic skills; ability to solve problems creatively and proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior knowledge of trading / capital markets is&amp;nbsp;not&amp;nbsp;required. Curiosity and a willingness to learn is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our tech stack includes an ever-evolving range of systems and technologies, and our engineers have the freedom to choose the best solution for the problem at hand. If a new technology has the potential to add value, we’ll actively invest in exploring, adopting and developing it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;At IMC, technology is not a department; it’s at the heart of everything we do. Developed in house, our innovative software makes millions of trading decisions daily, and we win by making better and faster decisions than our competition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IMC’s Amsterdam-based Java teams work on a wide variety of applications, tools and functionalities, including trading algorithm implementations, option pricing, calculating volatility, simulation frameworks, market risk applications, trade reconciliation applications and data analysis &amp;amp; visualisation tools for traders. We frequently need to develop not just the business applications themselves, but also the tools that keep our development process at the cutting edge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Core Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer, you’ll work in multidisciplinary teams alongside other engineers as well as risk teams and traders to deliver challenging projects, while taking ownership for end-to-end product development – from requirements gathering to production. You’ll write reliable, high-performance software while balancing time to production with quality and testability. Advanced automated testing and daily deployments will allow you to achieve agile and incremental benefits. Within a complex landscape of varying systems and technologies, you’ll be constantly challenged to consider trade-offs between latency, throughput, simplicity, scalability and maintainability. Your core tasks will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coding, developing, testing, deploying and maintaining applications and automations for Trading Teams and/or Risk Management, Mid-Office and Strategy Development Teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working through internal client requests. Gathering details, requirements and feedback from a range of internal stakeholders in order to implement creative automation solutions using innovative coding practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5+ years of experience as a Software Engineer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Java 17+. Experience in the latest versions of Java is highly desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Docker and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience gathering business requirements, communicating with key stakeholders and delivering solutions quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability able to work on greenfield projects under minimal supervision and to take full ownership of the applications you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high degree of flexibility and adaptability: willing and able to deal with uncertainty and ambiguity in a rapidly evolving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting and diagnostic skills; ability to solve problems creatively and proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MUST have passport valid for US (ESTA) and Australia (ETA/eVisitor or visa) business trips.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our tech stack includes an ever-evolving range of systems and technologies, and our engineers have the freedom to choose the best solution for the problem at hand. If a new technology has the potential to add value, we’ll actively invest in exploring, adopting and developing it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role in Our Story:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;As a Senior BI/Data Engineer at ACT, you will play a key role in modernizing and scaling our enterprise Data Platform. Combining hands-on engineering with technical ownership, you will design reliable, scalable data solutions across data integration, modelling, analytics engineering and platform architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Beyond delivery, you will help shape our platform roadmap and engineering standards, with a focus on architecture, automation, performance, security and cost efficiency. Microsoft Fabric is an important part of our modernization journey, alongside technologies such as Databricks where they add value. You will also have the opportunity to explore practical applications of Generative AI across development, documentation and platform operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value ownership, collaboration, knowledge sharing and continuous improvement. In essence, your role involves:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously improve key components of ACT’s Data Platform architecture and engineering standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement integrations for new source systems and build reliable, maintainable data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and document enterprise data models, including relational and dimensional models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, optimize and operate data pipelines and orchestration using technologies such as Azure Data Factory, Microsoft Fabric, Azure Functions and Logic Apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute data migrations with appropriate validation, reconciliation, data-quality controls and operational monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the modernization of the Data Platform using Microsoft Fabric and, where appropriate, Databricks and other modern data technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain trusted semantic models that enable scalable Power BI reporting, analytics and emerging AI use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business requirements into sustainable technical solutions and communicate design choices clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate data and analytics solutions to business stakeholders and support adoption through clear documentation and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates with the following qualifications and attributes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Business Information Technology, Data Engineering or a comparable field, or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in data engineering, including substantial hands-on experience with Microsoft Azure or another major cloud platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with modern data platforms such as Microsoft Fabric, Azure Synapse Analytics, Databricks or Snowflake.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and practical experience with Python for data engineering, automation or testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern data architectures, including data warehouses, data lakes and Lakehouse patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data-modelling skills, particularly relational and dimensional modelling; familiarity with additional modelling approaches is beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design, troubleshoot and optimize data transformations, SQL workloads and data pipelines for performance, reliability and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Power BI, semantic models or comparable analytics and visualization technologies is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Git, automated testing and CI/CD practices for data and analytics solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relevant Azure services such as Azure Data Factory, Azure Functions, Logic Apps, Synapse Analytics or Azure Automation is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of streaming, event-driven architectures or real-time analytics is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative and proactive mindset, strong communication skills, and the ability to take ownership while continuously learning and sharing knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet these criteria and are ready to contribute your expertise to a dynamic and challenging environment, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
